Use case: **place an order**. Checks inventory, charges payment, saves order, sends confirmation email.

**Layered (N-tier)**

```java
// Controller
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/orders")
public class OrderController {
    @Autowired OrderService service;
    @PostMapping
    public ResponseEntity<Order> place(@RequestBody OrderRequest req) {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(service.placeOrder(req));
    }
}

// Service
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired OrderRepository repo;        // JPA type leaks
    @Autowired PaymentClient paymentClient;  // concrete class
    @Autowired JavaMailSender mailSender;   // Spring Mail type leaks

    @Transactional
    public Order placeOrder(OrderRequest req) {
        Order order = new Order(req);
        paymentClient.charge(order);
        repo.save(order);
        mailSender.send(buildEmail(order));
        return order;
    }
}

// Repository
public interface OrderRepository extends JpaRepository<Order, Long> {}
```

Simple but: `OrderService` depends on `JpaRepository`, `JavaMailSender`, concrete `PaymentClient`. Unit testing service = pulling in Spring or mocking Spring types. Swapping JPA for DynamoDB = rewrite service.

**Hexagonal**

```java
// Domain / Use Case — depends only on ports
public class PlaceOrderUseCase {
    private final OrderRepository repository;         // port
    private final PaymentGateway paymentGateway;     // port
    private final NotificationSender notifier;        // port

    public PlaceOrderUseCase(OrderRepository r, PaymentGateway p, NotificationSender n) {
        this.repository = r; this.paymentGateway = p; this.notifier = n;
    }

    public Order execute(PlaceOrderCommand cmd) {
        Order order = Order.fromCommand(cmd);
        paymentGateway.charge(order.getTotal(), cmd.customerId());
        repository.save(order);
        notifier.sendOrderConfirmation(order);
        return order;
    }
}

// Ports (interfaces in domain module)
public interface OrderRepository { Order save(Order o); Optional<Order> findById(String id); }
public interface PaymentGateway { void charge(Money amount, String customerId); }
public interface NotificationSender { void sendOrderConfirmation(Order o); }

// Inbound adapter — REST
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/orders")
public class OrderRestAdapter {
    private final PlaceOrderUseCase useCase;
    public OrderRestAdapter(PlaceOrderUseCase useCase) { this.useCase = useCase; }

    @PostMapping
    public ResponseEntity<OrderDto> place(@RequestBody PlaceOrderRequest req) {
        Order order = useCase.execute(req.toCommand());
        return ResponseEntity.ok(OrderDto.from(order));
    }
}

// Outbound adapter — JPA implementation of OrderRepository port
@Repository
public class JpaOrderRepositoryAdapter implements OrderRepository {
    private final OrderJpaRepository jpa;
    public JpaOrderRepositoryAdapter(OrderJpaRepository jpa) { this.jpa = jpa; }

    @Override
    public Order save(Order o) {
        return jpa.save(OrderEntity.from(o)).toDomain();
    }
    @Override
    public Optional<Order> findById(String id) {
        return jpa.findById(id).map(OrderEntity::toDomain);
    }
}

// Spring config wires everything
@Configuration
public class Beans {
    @Bean
    PlaceOrderUseCase placeOrderUseCase(OrderRepository r, PaymentGateway p, NotificationSender n) {
        return new PlaceOrderUseCase(r, p, n);
    }
}
```

Domain module has zero Spring, JPA, or HTTP dependencies. Testable with POJOs. Swappable infrastructure. Costs: more files, explicit DTOs at boundaries, discipline to keep domain clean.

**Clean Architecture variant**

Same code structure as Hexagonal; rename 'Use Case' stays, 'Adapter' becomes 'Interface Adapter', add explicit 'Entity' layer for pure business objects. In Spring Boot, indistinguishable from hexagonal.

**Recommended package structure (hexagonal)**:

```
com.example.order/
  domain/
    model/       (Order, OrderLine, Money)
    port/        (OrderRepository, PaymentGateway, NotificationSender)
    usecase/     (PlaceOrderUseCase, CancelOrderUseCase)
  adapter/
    inbound/
      rest/      (OrderRestAdapter, dto)
      grpc/      (OrderGrpcAdapter)
    outbound/
      jpa/       (JpaOrderRepositoryAdapter, OrderEntity)
      stripe/    (StripePaymentGateway)
      sendgrid/  (SendgridNotificationSender)
  config/
    Beans.java
```
